Implement a retry loop for registering the D2P endpoint with the bootstrap server. This makes the startup process much more robust against temporary network issues or startup race conditions where the bootstrap server is not fully ready yet.

```python
        import time as _time
        for attempt in range(5):
            try:
                resp = _requests.put(
                    url,
                    json={"endpoint": self.d2p_receiver.endpoint},
                    timeout=10,
                )
                if resp.status_code == 200:
                    logger.info(
                        f"D2P endpoint registered: {self.d2p_receiver.host_port}"
                    )
                    return
                else:
                    logger.warning(f"D2P endpoint registration failed (status {resp.status_code}), retrying...")
            except Exception as e:
                logger.warning(f"D2P endpoint registration failed: {e}, retrying...")
            _time.sleep(1)
        logger.error("D2P endpoint registration failed after 5 attempts. D2P replication will not work.")
```
